WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.930
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:09.910
What are caustics?
A caustic is a beautiful phenomenon in nature

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:16.520
where curved surfaces reflect or refract light,
thereby concentrating it to a relatively small

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:17.400
area.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:23.380
It looks majestic, and it is the favorite
effect of most light transport researchers.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:29.369
You can witness it around rings, plastic bottles
or when you're underwater just to name a few

00:00:29.369 --> 00:00:29.829
examples.

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:34.559
If you have a powerful algorithm at hand that
can simulate many light transport effects

00:00:34.559 --> 00:00:41.120
than you can expect to get some caustics forming
in the presence of curved refractive or reflective

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:43.760
surfaces and small light sources.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:48.660
If you would like to know more about caustics,
I am holding an entire university course at

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:54.629
the Technical University of Vienna, the entirety
of which we have recorded live on video for

00:00:54.629 --> 00:01:00.510
you. It is available for everyone free of
charge, if you're interested, check it out,

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:02.809
a link is available in the description box.

00:01:02.809 --> 00:01:09.860
Now, the laws that lead to caustics are well
understood, therefore we can not only put

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:15.070
some objects on a table and just enjoy the
imagery of the caustics, but we can turn the

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:20.060
whole thing around: this technique makes it
possible to essentially imagine any kind of

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:24.890
caustic pattern, for instance, this brain
pattern, and it will create the model that

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:31.390
will cast caustics that look exactly like
that. We can thereby design an object by its

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:34.170
caustics.

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:52.850
It also works with sunlight, and you can also
choose different colors for your caustics.

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:57.570
This result with an extremely high fidelity
image of Albert Einstein and his signature

00:01:57.570 --> 00:02:02.770
shows that first, a light transport simulation
is run, and then the final solution can be

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:11.860
3D printed. I am always adamantly looking
for research works where we have a simulation

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:17.730
that relates to and tells us something new
about the world around us. This is a beautiful

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:29.760
example of that.

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:33.450
Thanks for watching and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

